[Music]  one of the best ways to watch the film  is like alone on a crappy VHS or some  old DVD player and I both knew that we  wanted the film to feel like a  documentary we shot the film  chronologically we had waypoints but  we're guided by GPS so they could  navigate through the woods without being  kind of hindered by a crew we shadowed  them as they were moving through the  trees then I kept away from them as much  as possible and there would be a bicycle  flag so when they got into the general  area of their Waypoint that's on their  GPS they could see the fly so that's  when they were instructed to pitch a  tent this is where you're camping for  the night and we had introduced plastic  milk crates and inside would be  foodstuffs fresh batteries for the  cameras own for the film camera and then  there would be these old-school  film canisters and inside those little  plastic containers would be directing  those and they were all instructed to  not read each other's notes so we set up  this conflict but we allow them to  choose the time when they want to have  it the mandate was just a role on  everything the name of the scene in the  script the confessionals it was the  moment the film where it stopped to be a  project about the Blair Witch and  started being a chronicling of their  last days on earth we were directing the  actress like their conscious speaking to  them for Heather is like you're  responsible for this I say your goodbyes  turn the camera light on and point the  camera at your face but give us  everything you got she took the camera  and walked off by herself and just had  this monologue to end all monologue  there was a lot more snot but there were  rivers and rivers of snot we wanted to  track a balance between the performance  and not getting too distracted with the  snot flow but I remember like for seeing  that monologue and our jaws dropped I  think that was the moment where we were  like wow this really could work we don't  screw it up we knew was something  special and we kind of made this little  bit of film history  [Music]

